[node name="Title" parent="Resources/Tab/HBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Resources"

[node name="Text" parent="Resources/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="0"]
text = "Currently, there are 3 resources in Babel.
 - [color=#71c548]Food[/color] [img]res://code/resources/miniResourceIcons/food.tres[/img] is used primarily to feed your population. If you run out of [color=#71c548]food[/color], the game ends.
 - [color=#fff]Earth[/color] [img]res://code/resources/miniResourceIcons/earth.tres[/img] represents building materials such as clay, mud, brick and stone and is primarily used for construction.
 - [color=#f00]Labor[/color] [img]res://code/resources/miniResourceIcons/labor.tres[/img] represents the working population of your civilization. [color=#f00]Labor[/color] per turn (the lower number) is used to power buildings. Free [color=#f00]labor[/color] (the higher number) is to power construction.
"

[node name="ChoiceTitle" parent="Resources/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Page 3"

[node name="Buildings1" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_lgwr8")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 1
anchors_preset = 8
anchor_left = 0.5
anchor_top = 0.5
anchor_right = 0.5
anchor_bottom = 0.5
offset_left = -160.0
offset_top = -160.0
offset_right = 160.0
offset_bottom = 160.0
grow_horizontal = 2
grow_vertical = 2

[node name="Title" parent="Buildings1/Tab/HBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Buildings (1)"

[node name="Text" parent="Buildings1/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="0"]
text = "Buildings are the primary way the player can produce and utilize their resources. 
There are a few types of buildings.
 - Static buildings produce and consume a fixed sum of resources all the time, and only stop when disabled.
 - Production buildings produce resources based on how many workers are assigned to them.
 - Adjacency buildings produce resources based on how many of a certain building they are adjacent to. 
Buildings cost Earth [img]res://code/resources/miniResourceIcons/earth.tres[/img] and [color=#f00]Labor[/color] [img]res://code/resources/miniResourceIcons/labor.tres[/img] to construct."

[node name="ChoiceTitle" parent="Buildings1/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Page 4"

[node name="Buildings2" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_lgwr8")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 1
anchors_preset = 8
anchor_left = 0.5
anchor_top = 0.5
anchor_right = 0.5
anchor_bottom = 0.5
offset_left = -576.0
offset_top = 16.0
offset_right = -256.0
offset_bottom = 228.0
grow_horizontal = 2
grow_vertical = 2

[node name="Title" parent="Buildings2/Tab/HBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Buildings (2)"

[node name="Text" parent="Buildings2/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="0"]
text = "To construct buildings, first navigate to the 'Build' tab near the bottom left corner.

Click 'Next' once you're in the 'Build' menu. You should be able to see the names of a few buildings... 'City', 'Farm', 'Kiln', etc."

[node name="ChoiceTitle" parent="Buildings2/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Page 5"

[node name="Buildings3" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_lgwr8")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 1
anchors_preset = 8
anchor_left = 0.5
anchor_top = 0.5
anchor_right = 0.5
anchor_bottom = 0.5
offset_left = -576.0
offset_top = -3.0
offset_right = -193.0
offset_bottom = 228.0
grow_horizontal = 2
grow_vertical = 2

[node name="Title" parent="Buildings3/Tab/HBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Buildings (3)"

[node name="Text" parent="Buildings3/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="0"]
text = "You'll notice that there is a building called 'Platform' which is unlike the others.
Platforms can be built above tiles (even ones with buildings on them) and can also be built upon each other. You can also construct buildings on platforms.
Now, select the 'Platform' button before continuing to the next part of the tutorial."

[node name="ChoiceTitle" parent="Buildings3/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Page 6"

[node name="Buildings4" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_lgwr8")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 1
anchors_preset = 8
anchor_left = 0.5
anchor_top = 0.5
anchor_right = 0.5
anchor_bottom = 0.5
offset_left = 64.0
offset_top = -92.0
offset_right = 320.0
offset_bottom = 260.0
grow_horizontal = 2
grow_vertical = 2

[node name="Title" parent="Buildings4/Tab/HBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Buildings (4)"

[node name="Text" parent="Buildings4/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="0"]
text = "You should now be able to see the Building Information menu. This menu will tell you everything about the building you have selected, like the cost, resources produced/consumed (if any), requirements for construction, etc. 
Below you can see the green 'Build' button with a hammer is disabled. 

Let's learn how to enable it. (Click 'Next')"

[node name="ChoiceTitle" parent="Buildings4/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Page 7"

[node name="Cursor" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_lgwr8")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 1
offset_left = 0.0
offset_top = 96.0
offset_right = 320.0
offset_bottom = 384.0

[node name="Title" parent="Cursor/Tab/HBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Cursor"

[node name="Text" parent="Cursor/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="0"]
text = "There should be a [color=#ff0]yellow[/color] outline shaped around the tile your cursor is hovering over. 
To select or deselect a tile, left click the screen. 
Select a tile with a building (or one adjacent to a building). The [color=#ff0]yellow[/color] outline turns [color=#f00]red[/color] when a tile is selected. It turns back when deselected. You can only select 1 tile at once.

Then, click 'Next' on the tutorial."

[node name="ChoiceTitle" parent="Cursor/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Page 8"

[node name="Buildings5" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_lgwr8")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 1
anchors_preset = 8
anchor_left = 0.5
anchor_top = 0.5
anchor_right = 0.5
anchor_bottom = 0.5
offset_left = 64.0
offset_top = -92.0
offset_right = 320.0
offset_bottom = 260.0
grow_horizontal = 2
grow_vertical = 2

[node name="Title" parent="Buildings5/Tab/HBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Buildings (5)"

[node name="Text" parent="Buildings5/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="0"]
text = "Hopefully now the green 'Build' button is no longer disabled. If it is, though, you can always identify why by hovering your mouse cursor over it and reading the tooltip. 

If the button is no longer disabled, then click it. You should now see a new platform building where on the tile you selected, and you may notice that your stored Earth [img]res://code/resources/miniResourceIcons/earth.tres[/img] and [color=#f00]Labor[/color] [img]res://code/resources/miniResourceIcons/labor.tres[/img] amounts have been consumed accordingly for constructing it."

[node name="ChoiceTitle" parent="Buildings5/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Page 9"

[node name="Heights" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_lgwr8")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 826.0
offset_top = 64.0
offset_right = 1152.0
offset_bottom = 421.0

[node name="Title" parent="Heights/Tab/HBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Heights (or, Layers)"

[node name="Text" parent="Heights/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="0"]
text = "You may have noticed that the up arrow on this 'Height' display lit up when you placed the 'Platform'. This is because you can now view another layer above the current one. 

You can navigate between heights using Q/E or the triangular buttons above this textbox. You start on Height 0 and unlock new heights when placing a platform on the highest 'height' you had up to that point.

Go ahead and navigate to Height 1 by pressing the 'E' key or the upwards facing triangle. Then press 'Next' to continue."

[node name="ChoiceTitle" parent="Heights/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Page 10"

[node name="Review1" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_lgwr8")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 446.0
offset_top = 215.0
offset_right = 702.0
offset_bottom = 467.0

[node name="Title" parent="Review1/Tab/HBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Review 1: Placing Buildings"

[node name="Text" parent="Review1/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="0"]
text = "Try placing a 'City' building on the 'Platform' you just placed.

If you are unsure how to do something, you can always review the previous pages of the tutorial by pressing 'Back' and navigating to the page you need."

[node name="ChoiceTitle" parent="Review1/Backdrop/MarginContainer/VBoxContainer" index="1"]
text = "Page 11 - Halfway there!"

[node name="Interact1" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_lgwr8")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 1
anchors_preset = 8
anchor_left = 0.5
anchor_top = 0.5
anchor_right = 0.5
